INT. AMATEUR THEATER GREEN ROOM - NIGHT

Costumes hang in clouds. Powder, hairspray, a half-eaten sandwich. A speaker on the wall hisses with the thin sound of an audience settling.

THEODORA "TEDDY" ALCOTT-WELLS (50s, tragedy mask on her forehead) stands at the mirror adjusting a Roman toga. Behind her, her understudy WILHELMINA "BILLIE" FAIRCHILD (20s, script clutched like a rosary) mouths lines to herself. Across the room, the director ALOYSIUS PENDERGAST-MWANGI (60s, cravat, velvet jacket) wrings his hands. At the costume rack, wardrobe mistress GWENDOLINE POPE (40s, pins in her mouth) hems a cape. Beside her sit the leading men: ARCHIBALD "ARCHIE" TREMAINE (30s, a laurel wreath), and RODERICK SPARROW-LUND (40s, a plastic sword).

THEODORA
She's late. Where is she?

ALOYSIUS
Who?

THEODORA
Calpurnia. The lead.

ALOYSIUS
She's in the lavatory.

THEODORA
She's been in the lavatory for forty minutes.

ARCHIE
Maybe she fell in.

RODERICK
That's not funny, Archie.

ARCHIE
It's a little funny.

GWENDOLINE
(through pins)
Hold still, Teddy.

THEODORA
I am still.

BILLIE
Mr. Pendergast-Mwangi, I know her lines.

ALOYSIUS
Darling, you are an understudy.

BILLIE
I'm a good understudy.

RODERICK
She really is, Aloysius.

ARCHIE
She did the balcony scene in her sleep last week.

ALOYSIUS
Because that is an excellent use of sleep.

The speaker hisses louder: the house lights dim, applause rises.

THEODORA
Aloysius, she's not coming.

ALOYSIUS
She will.

THEODORA
She will not.

GWENDOLINE
She will if I go and get her.

She spits the pins into her palm and marches out.

ARCHIE
Billie, you're up.

BILLIE
Me?

RODERICK
Take the wreath.

Archie lifts the wreath off his own head and lowers it onto hers. She stares into the mirror. Her hands stop shaking. Gwendoline sails back in, towing a tearful woman in a bathrobe.

GWENDOLINE
Here she is.

Billie and the woman in the bathrobe look at each other, and Billie hands back the wreath without a word.
